<%# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Logo mark — a raven perched on a cut ruby.

  Baltimore's bird (Poe's raven, not the NFL mark — no helmet, no shield, no
  purple) on the Ruby language's stone. Decorative: the wordmark beside it
  carries the name, so this is aria-hidden.

  Locals:
    classes — Tailwind sizing, default "h-8 w-8"
    uid     — id prefix, default "logo". MUST be unique per render on a page:
              the gradient and the two reused paths are referenced by id, and
              two marks on one page (header + footer) would otherwise collide.

  Construction, on a 64x64 grid, back to front:
    1. HALO. The raven, the legs and the gem outline are re-stroked in
       marble-50 at 2.4u BEFORE anything is filled, leaving ~1.2u of light
       outside every edge. On the marble page ground it is invisible; on the
       harbor-950 header and footer it becomes a rim that stops a dark bird
       dissolving into a dark bar. This is why one file works on both grounds
       and the mark needs no light/dark swap.
    2. GEM. Six flat facets, lit from the upper left: ruby-400 left,
       ruby-500 centre, ruby-600 right, plus one 30% marble glint.
       Table y=41, girdle y=47, culet 32,60.5.
    3. LEGS. 3.4u shanks, 2.4u toe bars — deliberately fat so they survive
       the downscale to favicon sizes as at least a smudge.
    4. RAVEN. One closed path: bill tip 6,18.5 / bill base 17.5,12.5 /
       crown apex ~24,6 / nape 31.6,17 / shoulder 45,23.5 / tail 56.5,31.5 /
       belly 29,37.6 / throat 15.5,23.5, then four short L segments for the
       hackles (blocky on purpose — anything finer turns to mush below 32px).
       The tail underside is a Q bowing UP toward the tip; that curve is the
       whole difference between a wedge tail and a rectangular plank.
       Plume gradient is weighted light (harbor-700 holds to 68%) so the halo
       reads as a rim rather than carrying the whole shape.
    5. EYE. One gold-300 disc. The only warm note on the bird.

  Everything sits in a 0.95 scale about the centre for optical breathing room;
  change that one number to tighten or loosen the mark inside its box.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------- %>
<% uid = local_assigns.fetch(:uid, "logo") %>
<svg class="<%= local_assigns.fetch(:classes, "h-8 w-8") %>"
     viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
  <defs>
    <linearGradient id="<%= uid %>-plume" x1="0.1" y1="0" x2="0.6" y2="1">
      <stop offset="0"    stop-color="#143f4e" />
      <stop offset="0.68" stop-color="#0b232c" />
      <stop offset="1"    stop-color="#06161c" />
    </linearGradient>
    <path id="<%= uid %>-raven"
          d="M6 18.5
             Q10.5 15.6 17.5 12.5
             C19 5.5 27.5 4.2 31 13
             L31.6 17
             C37 18.2 41.4 20.3 45 23.5
             L56.5 31.5 L54.5 35
             Q48 32.2 41.5 30.5
             C38 34.5 34 37.6 29 37.6
             C24 37.6 20.5 35 18.5 31
             C16.5 28.5 15.5 26 15.5 23.5
             L11.8 25.2 L16.4 23.2 L12.6 21.4 L16.5 19.5 Z" />
    <path id="<%= uid %>-gem" d="M17.5 41 L46.5 41 L53 47 L32 60.5 L11 47 Z" />
  </defs>

  <g transform="translate(32 32) scale(0.95) translate(-32 -32) translate(0.75,-0.5)">
    <%# 1. halo, drawn first so every fill lands on top of it %>
    <g fill="none" stroke="#fbf9f5" stroke-width="2.4"
       stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-linecap="round">
      <use href="#<%= uid %>-gem" />
      <path d="M25.6 35.6 L24.6 40.6 M31 35.6 L30.6 40.6" />
      <use href="#<%= uid %>-raven" />
    </g>

    <%# 2. the ruby %>
    <g>
      <path d="M17.5 41 L23.5 41 L20 47 L11 47 Z"   fill="#e0364a" />
      <path d="M23.5 41 L40.5 41 L43.5 47 L20 47 Z" fill="#c2182c" />
      <path d="M40.5 41 L46.5 41 L53 47 L43.5 47 Z" fill="#9b111e" />
      <path d="M11 47 L26 47 L32 60.5 Z"            fill="#e0364a" />
      <path d="M26 47 L38 47 L32 60.5 Z"            fill="#c2182c" />
      <path d="M38 47 L53 47 L32 60.5 Z"            fill="#9b111e" />
      <path d="M13.2 47 L19.4 47 L22.4 53.6 Z" fill="#fbf9f5" opacity="0.3" />
    </g>

    <%# 3. legs and toes %>
    <g stroke="#06161c" fill="none" stroke-linecap="butt">
      <path d="M25.6 35.6 L24.6 40.6 M31 35.6 L30.6 40.6" stroke-width="3.4" />
      <path d="M21.4 40.2 L28.6 40.2 M27.4 40.2 L34.2 40.2" stroke-width="2.4" />
    </g>

    <%# 4. the raven %>
    <use href="#<%= uid %>-raven" fill="url(#<%= uid %>-plume)" />

    <%# 5. eye %>
    <circle cx="21.5" cy="12.5" r="2.1" fill="#f6c85f" />
  </g>
</svg>
